larks:
Scarce known from evenings! also, let me say,
My larks fly higher than some windows. Right;
You’ve read your Leighs. Indeed ’twould shake a house,

Ye'll be glad for the glint o' its scarlet linin'
When the larks are up an' the sun is shinin';
When the winds are up an' ower the heather

lark:
While sorrow holds my mind;
I do not hear the lark,
For quenched is life's dear spark,--
